opennyai_summary.facts:
The present criminal revision has been filed to quash the order dated 27.02.2024 passed by the Juvenile Court / Special Judge (POCSO Act), Court No. 3, Ghaziabad in Criminal Appeal No. 19 of X Juvenile vs State Of U.P. on 8 July, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/36944595/
1 2024 (Kishore Apchari vs. State of U.P.) as well as judgment and order dated 16.01.2024 passed by the Juvenile Justice Board, Ghaziabad rejecting bail application no. 03 of 2024 arising out of Case Crime No. 61 of 2023 under Sections- 363, 366, 376 IPC and Section 3/4 of POCSO Act, Police Station- Shalimar Garden, District- Ghaziabad.
Learned counsel for the revisionist submits:
(i) admittedly, the revisionist was a juvenile on the date of alleged incident being 16 years and 03 months of age; he is in child protection home since 30.10.2023.
(ii) the revisionist has been falsely implicated;
(iii) there is no specific or strong objection raised in the DPO report, other than the general and vague observations;
(iv) there is no criminal history of the revisionist;
(v) there is no hope of early conclusion of the trial;
(vi) the revisionist has remained confined in the child observation home for an unduly long period of time;
(vii) none of the grounds contemplated under section 12 of the Juvenile Justice (Care and Protection of Children) Act, 2000 (hereinafter referred to as the Act) are available, to deny the bail to the revisionist.
